      <h2>Claude Code Plugin Marketplace</h2>
      <p>A Claude Code plugin marketplace with three plugins: metaskills for collaborative discovery, PRD creation and skill building, a software engineering audit, and a seedbox torrent controller.</p>

      <h3>Install</h3>
      <p>Add the marketplace, then install the plugin you want:</p>
<pre>
/plugin marketplace add liskl/claude-marketplace
/plugin install software-eng-laws@liskl-metaskills
/reload-plugins
</pre>
      <p>Swap <code>software-eng-laws</code> for any plugin name below.</p>

      <h3>software-eng-laws</h3>
      <p>Audits a repository against 56 software engineering laws (Conway, Hyrum, DRY, CAP, etc.) and writes a per-law findings report with evidence citations and a scorecard. Run it with <code>/software-eng-laws</code>.</p>

      <h3>metaskills</h3>
      <p>Slash commands for collaborative discovery, PRD creation and skill building.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>/metaskills:explore</code> - light, conversational discovery for new projects or features that surfaces the questions experienced collaborators ask before jumping to implementation.</li>
        <li><code>/metaskills:create-prd</code> - turns rough or detailed ideas into a structured PRD, adapting its depth to the input, in Obsidian-optimized or plain markdown.</li>
        <li><code>/metaskills:skill-builder</code> - an interview-driven generator that pulls tacit knowledge from a domain expert and emits a Claude Code skill or slash command.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>whatbox-rtorrent</h3>
      <p>Lists and controls torrents on a seedbox over rTorrent XML-RPC (<code>list</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>pause</code> and <code>resume</code>), in stdlib-only Python 3.10+ with nothing to <code>pip install</code>.</p>

      <p>The source is on GitHub at <a href='https://github.com/liskl/claude-marketplace'>liskl/claude-marketplace</a>.</p>

